+
+**Latest checkpoint 12 — September 10, 2026**
+
+- Added `tools/run_kicad_experiment.py`. It verifies frozen inputs, saves the
+  complete selected plan before running, and executes every primary and planned
+  rescue separately. Per-variant records retain commands, stdout/stderr, raw
+  output, parsed values, required/observed signals, statuses and comparison data.
+  A failed primary cannot be replaced by a successful rescue.
+- Added runtime preflight with analytical divider and POLY probes. Both pass
+  with the explicit system ngspice 42 startup. An actual negative control with
+  code models absent passes the divider but fails POLY and is rejected before
+  corpus work. Runtime records include binary/library/startup hashes, reference
+  version, environment choices and runner hashes. OSDI and dynamic/recursive
+  startup dependencies are not certified by these checks.
+- All **67,359 planned fixtures** pass required-observable extraction. Public
+  signals are required in both results even when both omit the same signal;
+  public names that resemble internal nodes still receive value comparisons.
+  Existing symmetric additive corpus tolerances are unchanged.
+- **335 Python/tooling tests pass, no skips.** Regressions cover partial raw data,
+  reported errors, timeouts, failed preflight, retained failed rescues, provenance
+  mutation and bounded work submission. The runner leaves an incomplete record
+  when input/runtime/source changes prevent trustworthy completion.
+- Final end-to-end smoke: three predetermined cases, five fixtures. Primary:
+  two MATCH and one NG_ONLY. Rescue: one MATCH and one NG_ONLY. RFF70N06 fails
+  neospice in both variants; these failures and all raw evidence are retained.
+  No engine, binding, C++ test or installed-wheel rebuild was needed this turn.
+- Acquired the official ngspice 47 release archive and verified its published
+  SHA-256. Source file hashes are retained in the acquisition record. It has
+  not been built or used as a numerical reference yet.
+
+**Full ngspice 42 run complete and reconciled:** all **67,359 fixtures** finished,
+with **650,116 retained artifact files** checked against their recorded hashes.
+Each planned case/variant has exactly one comparison record; no missing or extra
+records were found. The run used eight workers and a 10-second per-simulator
+timeout. It is operating-point compatibility evidence, not a benchmark.
+
+| Outcome | Primary (34,908) | Isolated/driven (32,451) |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| MATCH | 20,218 | 22,647 |
+| MISMATCH | 1,063 | 1,302 |
+| NG_ONLY | 1 | 22 |
+| NEO_ONLY | 4,950 | 7,152 |
+| NEO_TRIVIAL | 5,347 | 0 |
+| BOTH_FAIL | 3,329 | 1,328 |
+
+Primary agreement is 95.00% conditional on both simulations succeeding, or
+57.92% matched coverage of all primary cases. **10,342 primary MATCH cases have
+all node voltages below the historical 1e-6 V triviality threshold in both
+simulators**. These are not meaningful excitation certificates. Rescue agreement
+is 94.56% conditional, or 69.79% of its distinct population. Do not combine the
+populations or call reference failures neospice correctness wins.
+
+The 22 rescue NG_ONLY results include repeated model families, RFF70N06 and one
+neospice timeout. They were previously liable to disappear under success-only
+rescue adoption. Their retained circuits/errors need binding and numerical
+triage; they are not yet 22 independently established engine defects. The
+original six CTest failures remain separate, unresolved evidence.
+
